{
  "_comment": [
    "`klt sim` request for tb_adc_block_pex.spice -- issue #428 (T1 item 7).",
    "Consumed by `klt pex` through layout/adc-top/parasitics/run_pex_adc_block.py,",
    "which stages a copy of this file and rewrites `models` to the resolved PDK's",
    "absolute model-library path (the PDK-relative form below is the portable",
    "statement of WHICH library; see run_pex_comparator.py's _stage_request for",
    "why the absolute rewrite is needed on the extracted side).",
    "",
    "Corner matrix: the repo's FULL corner set (sim/harness/corners.py",
    "CORNER_SETS['full'] -- 5 MOS corners + 6 capacitor skews + 2 resistor",
    "skews, section bundles copied verbatim from that module) x the harness's",
    "default supply (+/-10 % about 3.3 V) x temperature (-40/27/125 C) axes =",
    "117 PVT points per side. supply_v moves V_dd, V_ref (= V_dd), V_cm",
    "(= V_dd/2) and the +/-250 mV input about V_cm together, by index.",
    "",
    "Measurements: `vres_diff`/`vtop_cm` carry NO limits on purpose -- no",
    "ratified spec row is stated at this block boundary for the raw residue,",
    "and inventing one here would be relaxing-or-tightening the spec by the",
    "back door. They are reported as schematic-vs-extracted DELTA rows, which",
    "is what T1 item 7 asks for. `dout_end`/`doutb_end` carry the one limit",
    "this stimulus does define: with V_inp > V_inn the DR-0014 residue is",
    "negative, so the comparator must resolve dout LOW and doutb HIGH (rail",
    "thresholds at 10 % / 87.5 % of the LOWEST swept supply, 2.97 V)."
  ],
  "netlist": "tb_adc_block_pex.spice",
  "engine": "ngspice",
  "models": {
    "pdk": "gf180mcuD",
    "lib": "libs.tech/ngspice/sm141064.ngspice"
  },
  "corners": {
    "process": [
      {
        "name": "tt",
        "sections": [
          "typical",
          "res_typical",
          "bjt_typical",
          "diode_typical",
          "moscap_typical",
          "mimcap_typical"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "ff",
        "sections": [
          "ff",
          "res_ff",
          "bjt_ff",
          "diode_ff",
          "moscap_ff",
          "mimcap_ff"
        ]
      },
      {
